From 3129948d0f0579f10484415e065503a977abd150 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:53:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] aera: draw transforms through layers, not the unsupported
 matrix

LV_DRAW_TRANSFORM_USE_MATRIX needs a draw unit that applies
lv_draw_task_t::matrix (vg_lite, nanovg). AERA's renderers are the SW
unit and the OpenGL ES unit, and neither reads it. With the option on,
every object with a transform style and full opacity goes through
refr_obj_matrix(), so:

- the transform is never drawn: transform_scale on pressed buttons,
  quick tiles, Recents cards, the power transition and enlarged icons
  renders at 100%;
- the clip area is widened by the inverse transform (refr_obj_matrix)
  but drawing stays untransformed, so children outside the screen are
  blended outside the display buffer. A Recents card or tile row that
  runs past an edge while shrunk on press, redrawn in full (opening
  Recents, rotating), crashes recovery with SIGSEGV in
  lv_draw_sw_blend (NULL from lv_draw_buf_goto_xy).

With the option off, LVGL draws such objects into a transform layer and
blends it scaled (SW unit; the OpenGL ES unit scales layer textures in
blend_texture_layer), which is what the styles ask for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J6XhHxrkhAcXmkzHMeCnVz
---
 lv_conf.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lv_conf.h b/lv_conf.h
index 233049659..5076e8818 100644
--- a/lv_conf.h
+++ b/lv_conf.h
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 #define LV_USE_GESTURE_RECOGNITION 0
 #define LV_USE_FLOAT 1
 #define LV_USE_MATRIX 1
-#define LV_DRAW_TRANSFORM_USE_MATRIX 1
+#define LV_DRAW_TRANSFORM_USE_MATRIX 0
 
 #define LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_14 1
 #define LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_16 1
